"""Indicates the state of a message from a subscription."""
enum MessageState {
    """The start of the messages for a given group of messages."""
    START
    """An update to an existing group of messages."""
    UPDATE
    """The ending of an existing group of messages."""
    END
}

"""Indicates the state of a message from a `devices` subscription."""
enum DeviceMessageState {
    """A new device is created."""
    CREATE
    """A device is updated."""
    UPDATE
    """A device receives a new `lastHeartbeat`."""
    HEARTBEAT
}

"""
How an update changes a `JSON` field. Give exactly one of `merge` or `replace`. To clear the field,
pass `null` for the whole input instead.
"""
input JSONUpdateInput @oneOf {
    """
    Merged into the stored value as a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7396):
    objects merge key by key, recursively; a key set to `null` is removed; any other value, arrays
    included, replaces the stored one. A stored value that is not an object is treated as `{}`. A
    `merge` value that is not an object replaces the stored value. Concurrent merges that touch
    different keys all persist.
    """
    merge: JSON
    """Replaces the stored value."""
    replace: JSON
}

"""
How an update changes a list of IDs. Give exactly one of `add`, `remove` or `replace`. To remove
every ID you can read, pass `null` for the whole input instead. IDs you cannot read are never
removed. Every ID given must exist and be readable by you.
"""
input IDListUpdateInput @oneOf {
    """
    Added to the list. Adding an ID already in the list does nothing. Concurrent adds all persist.
    """
    add: [ID!]
    """Removed from the list. Removing an ID not in the list does nothing."""
    remove: [ID!]
    """Replaces the IDs you can read. IDs you cannot read are kept."""
    replace: [ID!]
}

